ef 17592186420842 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420847 1069 "q-42578" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420847 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420847 1071 "Find $det({A}^{-1}),$ if $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 5\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420847 1072 #uuid "0b58d794-d6a1-55fe-88d5-660b59bdd30a" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420847 1074 "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet({A}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(A)}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $det(A):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =20-18 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\ndet({A}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(A)}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420848 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420841 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420848 1069 "q-43071" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420848 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420848 1071 "Find $det({A}^{-1}),$ if $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420848 1072 #uuid "37f105cd-9dd0-500b-bb29-7f9f80a1a14c" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420848 1074 "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet({A}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(A)}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $det(A):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =6-2 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\ndet({A}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(A)}=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420849 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420840 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420849 1069 "q-88281" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420849 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420849 1071 "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}],$ find $det(A).$" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420849 1072 #uuid "38d108f6-377b-5951-bc6b-4ec43d8b652b" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420849 1074 "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\ndet(A)=det[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot det[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that both matrices are triangular. Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =(3\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 2)\\cdot ((-1)\\cdot 3\\cdot (-4)) \\\\  & =(-6)\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =-72.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420850 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420846 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420850 1069 "q-42577" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420850 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420850 1071 "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],$ find $det(A).$" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420850 1072 #uuid "7f0a84be-936b-55f9-b169-54a768974c12" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420850 1074 "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\ndet(A)=det[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot det[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe can compute the required determinants as follows:\n\n- For the first determinant, we can compute it using a Laplace expansion across the $3$rd row.\n\n- For the second determinant, we can compute it using a Laplace expansion down the $2$nd column.\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|\\cdot 1(-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(2-1)\\cdot (8-6) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420851 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420845 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420851 1069 "q-88306" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420851 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420851 1071 "$|\\begin{aligned}300 & 250 & 100 \\\\ 300 & 270 & 100 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|=$" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420851 1072 #uuid "80589b9c-bfb0-57bc-8e70-de307d877343" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420851 1074 "First, notice that the $1$st row of our determinant is almost equal to the $2$nd row. So, we can rewrite the given determinant, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}300 & 250 & 100 \\\\ 300 & 270 & 100 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}300 & 250 & 100 \\\\ 300+0 & 250+20 & 100+0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, using the linearity property of determinants, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}300 & 250 & 100 \\\\ 300+0 & 250+20 & 100+0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}300 & 250 & 100 \\\\ 300 & 250 & 100 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}300 & 250 & 100 \\\\ 0 & 20 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first determinant must be zero since it has two identical rows, while the second determinant can be expanded across the $2$nd row, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}300 & 250 & 100 \\\\ 300 & 250 & 100 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}300 & 250 & 100 \\\\ 0 & 20 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =0+20(-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}300 & 100 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =20\\cdot (300\\cdot 1-100\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =20\\cdot 200 \\\\  & =4\\,000\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420852 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420843 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420852 1069 "q-130693" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420852 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420852 1071 "Find\n$|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 114 & 210 & 198 \\\\ 113 & 210 & 198\\end{aligned}|=$" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420852 1072 #uuid "8c3dc4f1-ad56-595b-a7eb-41a85271c7fe" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420852 1074 "First, notice that the $2$nd row of our determinant is almost equal to the $3$rd row. So, we can rewrite the given determinant, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 114 & 210 & 198 \\\\ 113 & 210 & 198\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 113+1 & 210+0 & 198+0 \\\\ 113 & 210 & 198\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, using the linearity property of determinants, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 113+1 & 210+0 & 198+0 \\\\ 113 & 210 & 198\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 113 & 210 & 198 \\\\ 113 & 210 & 198\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 113 & 210 & 198\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first determinant must be zero since it has two identical rows, while the second determinant can be expanded across the $2$nd row, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 113 & 210 & 198 \\\\ 113 & 210 & 198\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 113 & 210 & 198\\end{aligned}| & =0+1(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 210 & 198\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(4\\cdot 198-2\\cdot 210) \\\\  & =-(792-420) \\\\  & =-372\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420853 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420844 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420853 1069 "q-43070" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420853 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420853 1071 "Find $det({A}^{-1}),$ if $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 5\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420853 1072 #uuid "9e9ddda3-97aa-551d-9453-cae76713ec59" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420853 1074 "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet({A}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(A)}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $det(A):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =10-5 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\ndet({A}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(A)}=\\frac{1}{5}.\n$$" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420854 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420839 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420854 1069 "q-130474" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420854 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420854 1071 "Given that $C=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -6 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}],$ find $det(C).$" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420854 1072 #uuid "b1079762-fa86-56ef-a06d-de94245b17fa" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true] [17592186420854 1074 "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\ndet(C)=det[\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot det[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -6 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe can compute the required determinants as follows:\n\n- For the first determinant, we can compute it using a Laplace expansion across the $3$rd row.\n\n- For the second determinant, we can compute it using a Laplace expansion down the $2$nd column.\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =|\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -6 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\cdot (-1)(-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(6-4)\\cdot (-1)(12-5) \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-7) \\\\  & =-28.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534419 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0a0c86ff-0d80-5008-95a2-bec3a1c1a808" 17592186420799 "answer-11030227-d4ce-5b70-8894-186891176d6b" 17592186420800 "answer-15bb6772-ebfa-5300-9707-f0c44ba3ca38" 17592186420801 "answer-1657176b-b7bb-5bac-8681-50357708185d" 17592186420802 "answer-1de3d101-6ebd-5bbc-ad0b-5f1d9ed17bbf" 17592186420803 "answer-256655f5-3716-5c72-b038-769fa376cf93" 17592186420804 "answer-2f66b246-867d-5382-b745-224f4b0b1960" 17592186420805 "answer-336cb96e-8d35-5f9f-92e4-bf01f1fe608d" 17592186420806 "answer-341db512-89dd-5d60-9521-449fcc83f4d2" 17592186420807 "answer-3896dbb3-7bb1-5f7c-b8bf-88d4cf58a131" 17592186420808 "answer-3dafe486-15fc-5abc-8a0d-2beb22386f42" 17592186420809 "answer-44a67a7f-7ce3-5fc4-9a99-c7b43778cf51" 17592186420810 "answer-5725181a-ff3e-5107-8722-cd79c0a511e2" 17592186420811 "answer-65294e4c-a8db-5c12-befc-326f1199fa33" 17592186420812 "answer-6c92f4c3-474c-5da4-bd3e-a7ddf9353c60" 17592186420813 "answer-6f34b981-25b3-5127-9dcc-d184355dec85" 17592186420814 "answer-755ff62c-e4b0-56e4-8933-fdd296936d8f" 17592186420815 "answer-7dd0e1b8-d837-556e-96c2-a100f45e8fe7" 17592186420816 "answer-7ecdfc0d-790a-509f-8041-8c18f54a719a" 17592186420817 "answer-8e814c6a-3786-561d-9f46-38ef12a0585a" 17592186420818 "answer-90c1ce8c-7b18-5377-9a47-ace432f229bc" 17592186420819 "answer-9577d942-a37d-5bb6-ad63-4cff94938a48" 17592186420820 "answer-b440a564-08a1-5c84-a502-ec561384a59f" 17592186420821 "answer-b4fdf14b-3a08-5a96-9420-377d1a8d1538" 17592186420822 "answer-b74bd5d3-d00b-534f-908c-090b06c3201d" 17592186420823 "answer-b75e75d9-4872-5fbc-a